   $q$Which statement best describes the main distinction the author draws between Keiko and Rafael?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Keiko prefers to work alone at night, while Rafael prefers to paint in the busy morning.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Keiko is the more skilled painter, while Rafael is the more popular person in the town.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Keiko plans her whole design first, while Rafael lets his design grow from neighbors' ideas.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Keiko paints only scenes from nature, while Rafael paints only animals and old vehicles.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Keiko plans her whole design first, while Rafael lets his design grow from neighbors' ideas.$q$, $q$The author says Rafael "works the opposite way": Keiko sketches for six weeks, while Rafael starts with "only a rough idea" and adds what people remember. The subjects of the murals are details, not the main distinction.$q$, 'draft', '5488d23e-a3f0-5e96-809d-7ac41aab5d65')
